KG42.register("clusters-b2c7017cd659754ad9c9dabe",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v142-d-CL003","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","label":"Consumer-player classification and participation with no upper bound on the number of participants","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Consumer-player classification and participation with no upper bound on the number of participants","market_meaning":"Load entities may participate as independent consumers, including charging storage, NRL, and RLD. The number of consumer players is not limited by a numerical upper bound, and the same H-MG may accommodate consumers and generators at the same time.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"This expresses only consumer-role classification, permission on number, and the coexistence of roles within the same H-MG. The simulation setting of two players under the same ownership in each H-MG is not taken as a general participation condition. The absence of an upper bound on the number of participants also does not mean that other market conditions are waived.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Consumer-eligibility classification and permission on number have independent market meaning and need not be attached to a bidding or dispatch algorithm. Consumer cost objectives and dispatch mathematics are outside the scope declared by this cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"The single chain already gives the participating objects, the permission on number, and the result that roles coexist, which is sufficient to form a procedural candidate with an explicit scope."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G014","category":"unverified_source","description":"The consumer classification and the permission on the number of participants come from unaudited B entries. The boundary between the general role statements and the simulation assumptions still requires manual confirmation against the source.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-e033","v141-b-g02-e034"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the classification of consumer entities, the statement that there is no upper bound on the number of participants, and the way players are aggregated in the case. Keep the general rule separate from the ownership setting of the case."}]},"rule_refs":["33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-fc2134ec5ed3e3df"]});
